OL,4,CCentenarian sisters reunited after     
OL,5,Cfive years apart                       
OL,6,GCentenarian sisters Dot Rawlinson and  
OL,7,GBetty Blood have only been able to     
OL,8,Gkeep in touch through phone calls and  
OL,9,Gletters over the last five years.      
OL,11,FBut the siblings were finally able to  
OL,12,Fsit down and catch up on a lifetime of 
OL,13,Fmemories thanks to a reunion organised 
OL,14,Fby staff at Haddon Hall Care Home in   
OL,15,FBuxton, Derbyshire.                    
OL,17,FBetty, 101, who lives at the care      
OL,18,Fhome, spoke of being unable to see     
OL,19,FDot, 100, due to illness and because   
OL,20,Fshe lives at Bakewell Cottage Nursing  
OL,21,FHome, which is more than 10 miles away.
OL,22,                                   G2/4 
OL,23,D]CNews IndexG102CFlashG150CRegionalG160
